[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/564085050","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/8125#issuecomment-564085050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/8125","id":564085050,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDA4NTA1MA==","user":{"login":"appleby","id":86076,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MDc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86076?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby","html_url":"https://github.com/appleby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appleby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-12-10T15:26:17Z","updated_at":"2019-12-10T15:26:17Z","body":"As a workaround, if I manually \"flatten\" the `Union`, mypy is happy again. That is, the following typechecks even on mypy 0.750 / master\r\n\r\n``` python\r\nfrom typing import Union\r\n\r\nT3 = Union[int, float, complex]\r\n\r\ndef bar(a: T3, b: T3) -> T3:\r\n    return a + b  # ok\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/564085050/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"appleby","id":86076,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MDc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86076?v=4","gravatar_i